  "interpretation": {
    "primary_observation": "The local 7.2B model emitted only plan text for all 32 model turns, never invoked a repository tool, never edited a file, and reached the controller deadline on both cases.",
    "public_test_caveat": "RepoPilot's controller-owned public files passed at revision zero, but that is neither a fix nor SWE-bench resolution evidence.",
    "official_grading_caveat": "The official harness treats empty predictions as empty patches and does not execute FAIL_TO_PASS or PASS_TO_PASS tests for them. Both cases are therefore unresolved, with oracle test counts reported as unavailable rather than failed counts.",
    "deadline_caveat": "The current total deadline is checked between model turns and final controller collection still runs; in-flight calls and finalization produced bounded overshoots of 14.3 s and 31.9 s. This is a measured reliability limitation, not a security-boundary relaxation.",
    "model_caveat": "This pilot used a small local quantized model selected after the configured OpenAI credential failed a pre-run access check. Its outcome should not be generalized to stronger models or compared with leaderboard systems."
  },
  "known_limitations": [
    "Two selected instances are far too few for statistical or leaderboard claims.",
    "Both predictions were empty, so the official harness had no per-instance test execution and no FAIL_TO_PASS/PASS_TO_PASS pass counts.",
    "The local 7.2B Q4 model is not representative of frontier coding-agent models.",
    "One repetition per instance measures no run-to-run variance.",
    "The controller's deadline is soft between calls and finalization rather than a hard process kill.",
    "Localization precision is undefined for empty changed-file sets.",
    "Official grading metadata distinguishes empty patches from the harness's completed/unresolved buckets; this report maps them to unresolved at the pilot outcome layer."
  ]
